<p>Six items are new rules: change 37, a program's trait with its own <code>+</code> excludes <code>Number</code>; change 39, a type without its own <code>=</code> compares by strict equivalence; change 40, the static argument written where walk's printed type misleads; change 41, <code>Number</code> declares nothing; change 42, walk's float numerals under strict equivalence; change 48, a commit already made whose footer names a model is left as it is. Change 38 narrows a rule: the <code>Index</code> bound goes only into code that walk runs or that the checker checks against the interpreter's library. The other five state facts that the batch changed, and change no rule. Change 49 is not a new rule either: it defines two terms. Nor are the changes of 8 November to changes 37 and 39: change 37 now names the trait that excludes arrays and a third fix, and change 39 spells out strict equivalence and three cases where a worker would guess wrong.</p>
